<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Zähringen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zähringer</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Zähringen was a noble dynasty of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, named after Zähringen Castle near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freiburg-im-breisgau">Freiburg im Breisgau</a>. Its dukes founded towns including Freiburg im Breisgau, Fribourg and Bern, and governed much of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> as rectors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>. The main line died out with Berthold V in 1218, while a branch continued as the margraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-zahringen.jpg" alt="House of Zähringen" width="259" height="274" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz Zell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berthold_V,_Duke_of_Z%C3%A4hringen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
